## Steps

1. Write every exam, assignment deadline, class meeting, lab, office hour, and no-class day to
   {{run_dir}}/events.json as a JSON list with ONE EVENT PER LINE and no indentation, using a heredoc:
   cat <<'EOF' > {{run_dir}}/events.json
   [
   {"course": "CS 101", "title": "Quiz 2", "type": "exam", "date": "2026-10-14", "start": "09:00", "end": "09:50", "recurrence": null, "citation": "p.2: 'Quiz 2 - Wed 10/14 in class'", "confidence": "high"},
   ...one line like that per event, with all nine fields...
   ]
   EOF

   How to read a syllabus:
   - Class meetings come from the meeting line (e.g. "MWF 8:00-8:50", "TTh 9:30-10:50"): ONE event
     per meeting pattern with a weekly recurrence, not one event per lecture or per topic.
   - A schedule table of lecture topics (8.1, 8.2, "Intro", ...) is NOT a list of events. From it,
     take only exams, deadlines, and days with no class ("N/A", "no class", "holiday").
   - Each discussion/lab section is one weekly event.
