## Event format

Each event is a JSON object with exactly these fields. The values here only show the format;
take every event from the syllabus text above, never from this example.

{
  "course": "CS 101",
  "title": "Quiz 2",
  "type": "exam",
  "date": "2026-10-14",
  "start": "09:00",
  "end": "09:50",
  "recurrence": null,
  "citation": "p.2: 'Quiz 2 - Wed 10/14 in class'",
  "confidence": "high"
}

- course: {% if course %}use "{{course}}".{% else %}the course code as written in the syllabus, e.g. "CS 180" or "MATH 009C".{% endif %}
- type: one of exam, assignment, class, office_hours, other. Labs and discussion sections are "class".
- date: YYYY-MM-DD. Dates like "10/29" are in the term's year. Convert "Week 6 Thursday" with the week table.
- start / end: 24-hour "HH:MM", or null. A deadline "due 11:59 PM" has start "23:59" and end null.
  An all-day item (like a holiday) has both null.
- recurrence: null for one-time events. For a weekly meeting, an RRULE such as
  "FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,WE;UNTIL=20261204", and date is the FIRST meeting.
  BYDAY uses two-letter days: MO TU WE TH FR SA SU ("TTh" is TU,TH; "MWF" is MO,WE,FR).
  Use one event per weekly meeting pattern, not one event per week.
- citation: "p.N: '<exact words copied from the syllabus text>'". N is from the "=== page N ===" line above it.
  Copy the words exactly; they are checked against the text.
- confidence: "high" if the syllabus states the date clearly, otherwise "low".
